# Shopify Architecture & UI Constraints
- NEVER modify global CSS/SCSS files that affect the entire site unless explicitly instructed.
- Strictly use native Expanse theme UI components, utility classes, and CSS variables. Do not write custom CSS if a native utility exists.
- Do not remove or alter existing liquid logic related to core cart functionality or integrations outside of the exact requested scope.
- All new JavaScript must be vanilla JS (no jQuery) and must not block rendering.
- MANDATORY GIT WORKFLOW: After completing any significant code modification, refactor, or optimization step, create a atomic git commit with a clear conventional commit message (e.g., `perf: ...`, `fix: ...`, `feat: ...`) and execute `git push origin main`.
- Never leave large changes uncommitted or unpushed to the remote repository.
